WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.977
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:09.362
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:16.459
Unit nineteen: Making New Friends. In this unit, you will meet and welcome a new friend.

4
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.103
New.

5
00:00:18.803 --> 00:00:21.278
New means not seen or known before.

6
00:00:21.578 --> 00:00:22.974
We have a new student.

7
00:00:23.674 --> 00:00:26.234
Your turn. Say: New.

8
00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:29.633
New.

9
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:31.467
Friend.

10
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.584
Friend means a person you like and play with.

11
00:00:34.884 --> 00:00:36.698
Sokha is my best friend.

12
00:00:37.398 --> 00:00:40.027
Your turn. Say: Friend.

13
00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:43.519
Friend.

14
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:45.553
Introduce.

15
00:00:46.253 --> 00:00:49.100
Introduce means to tell people each other's names.

16
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.121
Let me introduce my friend.

17
00:00:51.821 --> 00:00:54.403
Your turn. Say: Introduce.

18
00:00:57.103 --> 00:00:58.139
Introduce.

19
00:00:59.150 --> 00:00:59.942
Name.

20
00:01:00.642 --> 00:01:02.967
Name means the word people call you.

21
00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:04.396
What's your name?

22
00:01:05.096 --> 00:01:07.167
Your turn. Say: Name.

23
00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:10.648
Name.

24
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.338
Play.

25
00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:15.374
Play means to have fun with games or toys.

26
00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.081
Let's play together!

27
00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:20.643
Your turn. Say: Play.

28
00:01:23.343 --> 00:01:24.030
Play.

29
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:25.913
Share.

30
00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:29.437
Share means to give part of something to someone.

31
00:01:29.737 --> 00:01:31.087
Can I share your book?

32
00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.729
Your turn. Say: Share.

33
00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.093
Share.

34
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:40.003
Smile.

35
00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:43.051
Smile means a happy look on your face.

36
00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:44.956
She has a big smile.

37
00:01:45.656 --> 00:01:48.238
Your turn. Say: Smile.

38
00:01:50.938 --> 00:01:51.754
Smile.

39
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.577
Welcome.

40
00:01:54.277 --> 00:01:57.542
Welcome means to say hello nicely to someone new.

41
00:01:57.842 --> 00:01:59.377
Welcome to our class!

42
00:02:00.077 --> 00:02:02.927
Your turn. Say: Welcome.

43
00:02:05.627 --> 00:02:06.431
Welcome.

44
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.683
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:13.613
Hello! Welcome to our class. What's your name?

46
00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:17.244
Hi, I'm Lina. I'm new here.

47
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.435
Nice to meet you, Lina! Do you like football?

48
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.645
No, but I like drawing.

49
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.893
Me too! Let me introduce you to my friends.

50
00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:33.486
Thank you, Rithy. You are very kind!

51
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:38.376
Grammar focus: What's your name? and Do you like ?.

52
00:02:38.676 --> 00:02:41.131
What's your name? Do you like football?

53
00:02:41.431 --> 00:02:45.277
Answer 'Do you like ...?' with 'Yes, I do' or 'No, I don't'.

54
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:48.912
Now read and listen. A New Classmate.

55
00:02:49.212 --> 00:02:52.350
Yesterday, a new student came to our class.

56
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:58.023
She looked shy, so I smiled and said, “Welcome! What's your name?”

57
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:02.408
Her name was Lina, and she liked drawing.

58
00:03:03.717 --> 00:03:05.763
I introduced her to my friends.

59
00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:11.186
At break time, we played together, and now we are good friends.

60
00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:15.182
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:15.482 --> 00:03:16.692
blank your name?

62
00:03:16.992 --> 00:03:20.564
A, What's. B, Where's. C, Who.

63
00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.654
The answer is A: What's.

64
00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.826
Do you like football? — Yes, I blank.

65
00:03:31.126 --> 00:03:33.757
A, do. B, like. C, am.

66
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.924
The answer is A: do.

67
00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:44.682
To say hello nicely to someone new is to blank.

68
00:03:44.982 --> 00:03:48.206
A, welcome. B, share. C, play.

69
00:03:52.217 --> 00:03:54.843
The answer is A: welcome.

70
00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:00.628
Now it's your turn to speak. How can you help a new student feel welcome?

71
00:04:05.928 --> 00:04:12.168
I can smile and ask, “What's your name?” Then I can introduce them to my friends and play together.

72
00:04:12.468 --> 00:04:14.061
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:20.306
Great work today! You learned eight new words and what's your name? and do you like ?.

74
00:04:20.606 --> 00:04:25.081
Today's value is friendliness. Smile and say hello to everyone.

75
00:04:25.381 --> 00:04:28.079
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

76
00:04:28.379 --> 00:04:30.858
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

